-- plus and minus on DateTime64
2023-06-01 18:10:01.312348	2023-06-01 18:10:01.112348	2023-06-01 18:10:02.712348	2023-06-01 18:09:59.712348	DateTime64(6, \'UTC\')
-- every combination of constant and materialized arguments
2023-06-01 18:10:01.312348	2023-06-01 18:10:01.312348	2023-06-01 18:10:01.312348	2023-06-01 18:10:01.312348
2023-06-01 18:10:01.112348	2023-06-01 18:10:01.112348	2023-06-01 18:10:01.112348	2023-06-01 18:10:01.112348
-- the number may also come first
2023-06-01 18:10:01.312348	2023-06-01 18:10:01.312348	2023-06-01 18:10:01.312348
-- addSeconds and subtractSeconds
2023-06-01 18:10:01.312348	2023-06-01 18:10:01.112348	2023-06-01 18:10:01.312348	2023-06-01 18:10:01.312348
-- common decimal fractions land on the exact tick
2023-06-01 18:10:01.300000	2023-06-01 18:10:01.700000	2023-06-01 18:10:01.290000	2023-06-01 18:10:01.070000
-- fractions a truncating implementation would get wrong
2023-06-01 18:10:01.29
2023-06-01 18:10:01.2
2023-06-01 18:10:01.001
2023-06-01 18:10:02.000000
-- the same fraction is kept whatever the whole part is
2023-06-01 18:10:01.2	2023-06-01 18:10:02.2	2023-06-01 18:10:03.2	1
2023-06-01 18:10:01.001	2023-06-01 18:10:02.001	2023-06-01 18:10:04.001
-- every scale
2023-06-01 18:10:03
2023-06-01 18:10:02.0
2023-06-01 18:10:01.124
2023-06-01 18:10:01.123457
2023-06-01 18:10:01.123456790
-- Float32 delta
2023-06-01 18:10:01.500000
-- a whole number of seconds given as a float is still exact
2062-07-15 17:41:31.123456789
2062-07-15 17:41:31.123456789
-- Time64
18:10:01.312348	18:10:01.112348	18:10:01.312348	Time64(6)
-- a String argument is parsed into a DateTime64(3)
2023-06-01 18:10:01.623	2023-06-01 18:10:00.623
2023-06-01 18:10:01.623
-- a column of deltas
2023-06-01 18:10:01.000000
2023-06-01 18:10:01.100000
2023-06-01 18:10:01.200000
2023-06-01 18:10:01.300000
-- the types that cannot represent a fraction of a second are unchanged
2023-06-01 18:10:01	DateTime(\'UTC\')
2023-06-01	Date
2023-06-01	Date32
18:10:01	Time
-- an out of range delta is rejected instead of being undefined
